---
// Differentiators.astro — the three-point pitch, from docs/product-vision.md.
// Glyphs are geometric SVG (currentColor), never emoji — lessons 2026-08-18.
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="diff-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">why it's different</p>
      <h2 id="diff-title">Three things no app platform gives you.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="diff-grid">
      <article class="diff">
        <svg class="diff-glyph" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="7" cy="14" r="4.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"></circle>
          <circle cx="21" cy="14" r="4.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"></circle>
          <path d="M11.5 14h5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>A runtime relationship, not codegen</h3>
        <p>
          Each app carries a compact <strong>runtime contract</strong> — what it is, what a good
          answer looks like — so its turns cost ~nothing and the same app runs well on a frontier
          model or a small local one. The agent plays chess with your app every move, forever.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="diff">
        <svg class="diff-glyph" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" aria-hidden="true">
          <path
            d="M6 4h12l4 4v16H6z"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.8"
            stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
          <path d="M10 15l3 3 5-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>One file. Yours.</h3>
        <p>
          Every app you build — code, versions, its own isolated database, its chats — lives in{' '}
          <strong>one portable <code>.snug</code> file</strong> (real SQLite, openable with ordinary
          tools, optionally sealed with a passphrase only you hold). Any hub, any LLM provider, sync
          where you choose. Leave whenever you like and take everything.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="diff">
        <svg class="diff-glyph" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect
            x="5"
            y="12"
            width="18"
            height="12"
            rx="2.5"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.8"></rect>
          <path
            d="M9 12V9a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v3"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.8"></path>
        </svg>
        <h3>Secure by construction</h3>
        <p>
          Apps run in a hard sandbox with <strong>zero network of their own</strong>. Your
          credentials never enter the app, never reach the LLM, never reach a publisher — every
          connected request goes through a host executor inside a ceiling you approved and the host
          froze.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="diff-more">
      <a href="/architecture/">See how it works — six diagrams →</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .diff-more {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  .diff-more a {
    color: var(--ember-bright);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .diff-more a:hover {
    color: var(--ember);
  }

  .diff-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .diff {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
  }

  .diff-glyph {
    color: var(--ember);
  }

  .diff h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-l);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .diff p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: var(--text-s);
  }

  .diff code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--ember-bright);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .diff-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
